PosternDEX: licences

This repository is not under one licence. Which licence governs a file depends on what the file derives from.
The details and the evidence are in docs/LICENSING.md; attributions are in NOTICE.

  Path                                   Licence              Full text
  -------------------------------------  -------------------  ------------------------------------
  contracts/  script/  test/             GPL-3.0-or-later     LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt
  everything else (frontend/, scripts/,  MIT                  LICENSES/MIT.txt (the same text follows)
  deployments/, docs/, top-level files)

contracts/, script/ and test/: the exchange contracts are a port of Uniswap V2 (v2-core and v2-periphery), which
their publisher licenses under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or any later version. A work derived
from GPL code can only be distributed under the GPL, so that licence governs those files, the other Solidity
files that are compiled together with them into the deployed contracts, and the deployment scripts and tests
that import them. The line "SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT" at the head of the files under contracts/ predates
this statement and does not change it: where that line and this file differ, this file governs. (The contract
sources are frozen byte for byte for the deployments in progress; the header lines are corrected at the next
revision of the contracts.) Copyright in the changes and additions made in this repository:

  Copyright (C) 2026 TBD-owner

  This program is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU General
  Public License as published by the Free Software Foundation, either version 3 of the License, or (at your
  option) any later version. This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY
  WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See the
  GNU General Public License for more details (LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt).

Third-party software is under its own licences: the packages the frontend bundles are listed with their licence
texts in frontend/public/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt (it ships with every build of the page). Two of them, Reown
AppKit and WalletConnect, are not open-source licences: see docs/LICENSING.md section 4.

